hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2794","###\n Narrated to us Muhammad bin Ma'mar, who said: Narrated to us Muhammad, meaning Ibn Bakr al-Bursani, who said: He informed us that Ibn Jurayj said: Abu az-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrating about the Farewell Pilgrimage of the Prophet (ﷺ). He said: After we had performed the Tawaf (circumambulation of the Ka'bah), the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded us to enter the state of Ihram ("
"2795","###\n Narrated to us by Bundar, who narrated to us from Ibn Abi 'Adi, from Dawud. [In another chain:] Narrated to us by Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid, who narrated to us from 'Abd al-A'la, who narrated to us from Dawud, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id (RA), who said: \"We went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) until, when we had performed the Tawaf of the"
